I built the issue desk in `app.contract` (the three-tab view) and `app.ts` (the data module, with an overlay for optimistic writes), in `/tmp/claude-0/runs/r15/desk9-contract-haiku-3`. `./check` passes, and `./test` passes all 30 visible tests. I also ran 15 temporary decline, failure and retry tests against the same app, and all passed; I then restored `tests/visible.mjs` to its original content. I used 6 of the 15 check/test runs.

I was least sure about two things. First, the Exact overlay is what makes rollback work, so a declined write disappears and the server's answer shows; I did not test that the fake backend's later answers match what the overlay keeps. Second, the assign decline shows the bare server message (`declined`), because the brief gives no prefix for it, and I read that literally.